sentences.l:
On them I a blackening cloud, mixed with hail,
while the wings are in tumult and the glades they ring with a net,
from above will pour, and with thunder the whole sky I shall stir.

sentences.t:
Postquam altos ventum in montis atque invia lustra,
ecce ferae, saxi deiectae vertice, caprae
decurrere iugis;

sentences.l:
After they came to the high mountains and the trackless haunts,
behold, wild goats, from the peak of a rock dislodged,
ran down the ridges;

sentences.t:
et Tyrii comites passim et Troiana iuventus
Dardaniusque nepos Veneris diversa per agros
tecta metu petiere;

sentences.l:
and the Tyrian companions on all sides and the Trojan youth
and the Dardan grandson of Venus, different through the fields
shelters in fear sought;
